      "id": "M4172-A",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "language": "en",
      "prompt": "Request A: Four same-unit entries have reference-observation mask R=(1,1,0,1) and known values (0,10,unknown,30). An independent evaluation deliberately withholds entry 2, so the supplied input-observation mask is M=(1,0,0,1). The imputer returns estimates z=(5,12,99,20). Finite input placeholders are used, not NaNs. Completion selects the supplied measurement where M=1 and z where M=0. Compute the completed vector, the mask of artificially withheld entries with known references, its count and its missing-entry MSE. Can either zero-valued observation or naturally unknown entry 3 be treated as a missing reference? Can scoring all known entries after reinserting measurements establish recovery accuracy at every missing entry? Separately distinguish an artificial missing-value target retained for training supervision inside the training partition from a held-out evaluation reference used only for scoring. Neither an observed-entry reconstruction loss nor a prefill operation automatically establishes unknown-entry accuracy. Masks in two papers may use opposite 1/0 conventions; do not borrow a complement from the name. Replacing numerical candidates and updating trained parameters are different operations. Check whether the Skill has a completed matched definition record for data/missing-value imputation and separately verified Chinese wording; absence does not mean invalidity. ",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Compute completion (0,12,99,30), known-hidden mask (0,1,0,0), count 1 and MSE 4; copied-observation all-known MSE is 4/3, not all-missing recovery.",
        "Retain observed zero, unknown natural reference, training versus scoring-only targets, actual mask meaning and existing P25/P33 admission while using added P106/P107 scoped contexts."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Invent reference truth for entry 3, equate prefill/reconstruction with recovery proof, or label legitimate hidden training targets leakage.",
        "Erase the already valid old admission, certify full networks or run experiments."
      ],
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill"
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "reason": "Correct completion/hidden-mask/count and MSE arithmetic; preserves observed zero and unknown natural reference, training versus evaluation targets, mask conventions and candidate/parameter distinctions. Retains old P25/P33 admission plus additional industrial and Chinese wording scopes.",
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4172-independent.md",
      "review_trace": "reviews/v4172-independent-evaluation.md",
      "evaluation_phase": "new_context_same_A_B_final_source"
