    {
      "id": "M4172-B",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "language": "en",
      "prompt": "Request B: A separate fictional verified industrial soft-sensing interface learns an imputer on incomplete training measurements using only observed-entry reconstruction targets, estimates unobserved auxiliary measurements, and explicitly merges estimates with available original measurements. The completed auxiliary inputs train a quality regressor on the available training quality labels. On each permitted test window both fitted components are frozen and produce a quality estimate; training reconstruction uses no naturally unknown ground truth and the evaluation references never guide fitting or selection. The imputer does not estimate the quality target directly. Give three concise reusable English prose blocks and separate proportional author/review notes: (1) a positive 40-65-word abstract/method chain connecting the imputer, merge and actual quality predictor; (2) a 20-40-word candidate contribution linking the input-availability requirement to that learning recipient without certifying routine imputation as novel; (3) a 20-35-word analytical-result description reporting only Request A's supplied hidden-entry result, not fabricated industrial performance. Preserve the legitimate observed-only imputer fitting and labeled downstream predictor without calling the entire pipeline unsupervised or prescribing this architecture for every missing-data paper. Exact model construction, selection details and unverified novelty/evidence belong in notes; do not invent online parameter learning or proof of naturally unknown recovery. State word/sentence counts. These are arithmetic/prose fixtures, not research experiments.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Write positive 40-65/20-40/20-35-word blocks connecting observed-target imputer fitting, measurement merge, labeled quality-regressor training and frozen permitted-test prediction.",
        "Keep only the supplied hidden-entry result; put unspecified construction/novelty/evidence in proportional author notes."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
